{#-
  Tells somebody their Quill account has been closed. Sent once, when it
  is closed, to everybody whose address was verified: it is usually an
  administrator who closes an account, so otherwise the first they would
  know is a login that no longer works. Neutral on purpose: it never
  says why.

  It says what happens to their data next, kept general, with a link to
  the privacy policy for the periods, so that it does not go out of date
  when a sponsor's period changes.

  The paragraph about news and updates is shown only when their stored
  answer is yes: they carry on, and a link in the sentence stops them.
  A link and not a button, Mark's decision: a large button is too
  tempting to press. Context:
    name                who to greet: their full name, or their username
                        where the account has none
    username            the account's username
    email               the address this is sent to, said back to them
    privacy_policy_url  the published privacy policy
    unsubscribe_url     the page that stops the newsletter, or none for
                        somebody who is not sent one
-#}
{% extends "base.html.j2" %}
{% import "_components.html.j2" as c with context %}

{% block subject %}Your Quill account has been closed{% endblock subject %}
{% block preheader %}You can no longer log in to it.{% endblock preheader %}

{% block body %}
{{ c.heading("Your account has been *closed*") }}
{{ c.paragraph("Hi " ~ name ~ ",") }}
{% call c.paragraph() %}Your Quill account, with the username <strong>{{ username }}</strong>, has been closed. You can no longer log in to it.{% endcall %}
{{ c.paragraph("If a sponsor gave you access, such as a training academy or an employer, it keeps its copy of your training records for its own period. The account itself is deleted two years after it was closed.") }}
{% call c.paragraph() %}Our <a href="{{ privacy_policy_url }}">privacy policy</a> says how long each kind of record is kept.{% endcall %}
{% if unsubscribe_url %}
{{ c.paragraph("You are set to receive news and updates from Quill Medical. Closing your account does not change that, so they will carry on arriving at this address.") }}
{% call c.paragraph() %}If you would rather they stopped, you can <a href="{{ unsubscribe_url }}">stop news and updates</a> now. Every newsletter also carries a link that does the same.{% endcall %}
{% endif %}
{{ c.small("This email was sent to " ~ email ~ ".") }}
{{ c.small("If you think your account was closed by mistake, speak to whoever looks after Quill where you work or train.") }}
{% endblock body %}

{% block reason %}You are receiving this because your Quill account was closed.{% endblock reason %}

{% block text %}
Hi {{ name }},

Your Quill account, with the username {{ username }}, has been closed. You can no longer log in to it.

If a sponsor gave you access, such as a training academy or an employer, it keeps its copy of your training records for its own period. The account itself is deleted two years after it was closed.

Our privacy policy says how long each kind of record is kept: {{ privacy_policy_url }}
{% if unsubscribe_url %}
You are set to receive news and updates from Quill Medical. Closing your account does not change that, so they will carry on arriving at this address.

If you would rather they stopped, you can stop news and updates now: {{ unsubscribe_url }}

Every newsletter also carries a link that does the same.
{% endif %}
This email was sent to {{ email }}.

If you think your account was closed by mistake, speak to whoever looks after Quill where you work or train.
{% endblock text %}
